Root cause:
The bug was caused by the inability to disable the audio component binding in the HDMI audio driver, which was necessary for debugging purposes. The recent regression indicated that there were scenarios where developers needed to turn off this feature without recompiling the kernel. The patch introduces a module parameter (`enable_acomp`) that allows users to easily enable or disable audio component binding, addressing the need for flexibility in debugging.
